    male|a||Suppose every state that adopts a policy gains from it, and the regression we all learned reports that the policy did harm.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8040
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'male|a||That can happen, and it happens for one reason: the states adopted in different years.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:xstpws'
    'male|a||Medicaid grew that way under the Affordable Care Act: after a Supreme Court ruling in 2012, each state chose whether, and when, to expand.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:ox63tx'
    male|a||So take two made-up states. Early expands in 2014, and Late waits until 2015.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:14na24s'
    male|a||The outcome is the share of low-income adults with insurance. Early goes from sixty, to sixty-four, to seventy-two percent.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:sb32d7'
    male|a||Late goes from fifty to fifty-two, and then to fifty-six in its first expanded year.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:cq2cm1'
    male|a||Red marks a year before a state expands, blue a year after, and the blue cells form a staircase. That staircase is the whole problem.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1gd3mc9'
    'male|a||Because these states are made up, we know what real data never shows: without expansion, each would have gained two points a year anyway.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:hr37s9'
    male|a||So expansion added two points in Early's first year, eight in its second as people kept enrolling, and two in Late's first year.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:160mxj7'
    male|a||Every effect is positive, and across the three expanded cells they average four percentage points.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:tb9b1j'
    'male|a||The standard tool is two-way fixed effects: a dummy for each state, a dummy for each year, and one coefficient, beta, on being expanded.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:17l8q0u'
    male|a||The state dummies soak up that Early simply has more coverage; the year dummies soak up the two points a year that everyone gains.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1ucrnhd'
    male|a||First, a guess. Every effect in the table is positive. What will two-way fixed effects report for beta hat?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1djzmhy'
    'male|a||Below zero: it comes out at minus one, though no state lost anything.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5600
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'male|a||Run it on these six numbers and beta-hat is minus one: expansion, says the regression, cut coverage by a percentage point.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8600
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||Yet no state lost a single point. So the regression is comparing something other than what we meant, and the way to find out what is to take beta-hat apart.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:t1h24q'
    male|a||Where does minus one come from? With two states and three years, the regression is an average of two small difference-in-differences comparisons.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9800
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||The first runs from 2013 to 2014. Early expands; Late has not yet.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:9gim3k'
    'male|a||Early gains four points and Late gains two, so the difference is two: exactly Early''s true first-year effect.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1n9xo2v'
    'male|a||Late is a clean control here: in 2014 it is still untreated, so its change is the trend alone.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1vgyjqt'
    male|a||The second runs from 2014 to 2015. Now Late expands, and the only state left to compare it with is Early, which expanded a year before.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:e42qbx'
    male|a||Late gains four, Early gains eight, and the difference is minus four.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:14xuktr'
    male|a||But Early's eight is not the trend. It is two points of trend plus six points of its own effect, still growing from two to eight.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:3g646f'
    'male|a||So this comparison subtracts Early''s growing effect from Late''s: an already-treated state has quietly served as the control.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1bnmpm4'
    male|a||Here the two comparisons get equal weight, and two and minus four average to minus one, the number the regression gave.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:7a4nyp'
    'male|a||And this is no quirk of two states: Andrew Goodman-Bacon showed in 2021 that any two-way fixed effects estimate with staggered timing is such a weighted average, with weights set by group sizes and by when in the panel each group switched.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 15520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1vanl56'
    male|a||Written in true effects instead, our beta-hat is Early's first-year effect, plus half of Late's, minus half of Early's second-year effect.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:gqpow0'
    male|a||The largest effect in the table enters with a minus sign. De Chaisemartin and D'Haultfœuille, in 2020, called these negative weights, and they come from using already-treated states as controls.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 11600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:whfja8'
    male|a||A new case. Suppose Early's effect had stayed at 2 in its second year, with everything else the same. What would beta hat be?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:uo9lnu'
    'male|a||Two: Early''s change from 2014 to 2015 is then the trend alone, so the second comparison is clean too and gives two.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8520
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'male|a||So the damage comes from one thing: an effect that changes after a state has switched on.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6240
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||Watch Early's second-year effect run from zero to ten, and beta-hat fall as it rises.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:ibye7n'
    male|a||At two, beta-hat is two, the truth. Every point Early's effect grows takes half a point off, and at six beta-hat reaches zero.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10360
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||Constant effects leave the regression honest. Effects that build, as coverage does while people enrol, turn it against itself.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:11wmq88'
    'male|a||The repair is simple to state: never let an already-treated state play the control.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6040
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'male|a||Callaway and Sant''Anna, in 2021, build the estimate from one small effect at a time: ATT of g and t, the average effect for the group that expanded in year g, in calendar year t.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 14560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:f6gis3'
    'male|a||Its missing half, the outcome without expansion, is borrowed from a state that has not been treated: one that never expands, or one that has not expanded yet.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:11l25ht'
    male|a||Check the table. In the two-state table, which effects have a clean control, a state still untreated that year?:
